---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site, addressLines } from '../config/site';

const { legal } = site;
const company = legal.entityName;

const toc = [
	{ id: 'commitment', title: 'Our commitment to client satisfaction' },
	{ id: 'when-a-refund-may-be-requested', title: 'When you may request a refund' },
	{ id: 'how-to-request-a-refund', title: 'How to request a refund' },
	{ id: 'opportunity-to-resolve', title: 'Opportunity to resolve the issue' },
	{ id: 'full-or-partial-refunds', title: 'Full or partial refunds' },
	{ id: 'refunds-for-completed-work', title: 'Refunds for completed work' },
	{ id: 'client-requested-changes', title: 'Client-requested changes' },
	{ id: 'client-responsibilities', title: 'Client responsibilities and delays' },
	{ id: 'third-party-services', title: 'Third-party services and costs' },
	{ id: 'subscription-services', title: 'Subscription and recurring services' },
	{ id: 'deposits-and-payments', title: 'Deposits and project payments' },
	{ id: 'refund-processing', title: 'Refund processing' },
	{ id: 'chargebacks', title: 'Chargebacks and payment disputes' },
	{ id: 'no-waiver', title: 'No waiver of legal rights' },
	{ id: 'final-determination', title: 'Final refund determination' },
	{ id: 'good-faith-requests', title: 'Good-faith refund requests' },
	{ id: 'contact-us', title: 'Contact us' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
	title="Refund & Satisfaction Policy"
	intro="At Linkly LLC, we are committed to delivering high-quality software development, web applications, mobile applications, AI solutions, automation systems, and related technology services. Our goal is to build long-term relationships with our clients through transparency, accountability, and reliable delivery."
	lastUpdated="October 6, 2026"
	toc={toc}
	seo={{
		title: 'Refund & Satisfaction Policy',
		description:
			'Linkly LLC refund and satisfaction policy for custom software, AI, web, and mobile projects.',
	}}
>
	<p>
		We understand that software projects can evolve and that issues may occasionally
		arise. If you are not satisfied with our services, we encourage you to contact
		us so that we have an opportunity to understand the concern and work toward a
		fair resolution.
	</p>

	<h2 id="commitment">1. Our Commitment to Client Satisfaction</h2>
	<p>
		Linkly LLC stands behind the work we deliver.
	</p>
	<p>
		If our delivered services materially fail to meet the requirements expressly
		agreed upon in the applicable proposal, Statement of Work ("SOW"), contract,
		or project agreement, we will make reasonable efforts to correct the issue at
		no additional cost when the issue falls within the original agreed scope.
	</p>
	<p>
		If the issue cannot reasonably be resolved and the client remains dissatisfied,
		Linkly LLC may provide a <strong>partial or full refund</strong>, depending on
		the circumstances, work completed, payments received, and applicable agreement.
	</p>

	<h2 id="when-a-refund-may-be-requested">2. When You May Request a Refund</h2>
	<p>A client may request a refund if:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>The delivered work materially fails to match the agreed project requirements.</li>
		<li>A significant portion of the agreed services has not been delivered.</li>
		<li>Linkly LLC is unable to complete a material portion of the agreed scope.</li>
		<li>A material defect or issue cannot reasonably be corrected within the agreed scope.</li>
		<li>Linkly LLC and the client mutually agree to terminate the project.</li>
		<li>Other circumstances justify a refund under the applicable agreement or applicable law.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		Refund requests must be made in good faith and should identify the specific
		deliverables, functionality, or services that are the basis for the request.
	</p>

	<h2 id="how-to-request-a-refund">3. How to Request a Refund</h2>
	<p>Refund requests must be submitted in writing to:</p>
	<p>
		<strong>Email:</strong>
		<a href="mailto:payment@linklyLLC.com">payment@linklyLLC.com</a>
	</p>
	<p>The request should include:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Client or company name</li>
		<li>Project name</li>
		<li>Relevant invoice, proposal, or SOW, if available</li>
		<li>Description of the issue</li>
		<li>Specific deliverables or functionality involved</li>
		<li>Reason the delivered work does not meet the agreed requirements</li>
		<li>Any relevant supporting information</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		We may request additional information or schedule a discussion with the client
		before making a final determination.
	</p>

	<h2 id="opportunity-to-resolve">4. Opportunity to Resolve the Issue</h2>
	<p>
		Before issuing a refund, Linkly LLC will generally be given a reasonable
		opportunity to resolve the issue.
	</p>
	<p>Depending on the circumstances, we may:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Correct bugs or defects;</li>
		<li>Make reasonable revisions;</li>
		<li>Adjust functionality to match the agreed requirements;</li>
		<li>Rework affected deliverables;</li>
		<li>Provide additional clarification or technical support; or</li>
		<li>Propose another mutually reasonable solution.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		Our preferred approach is to resolve legitimate concerns and complete the
		project successfully rather than immediately terminate the engagement.
	</p>

	<h2 id="full-or-partial-refunds">5. Full or Partial Refunds</h2>
	<p>
		If a refund is approved, the refund may be <strong>partial or full</strong>,
		depending on the circumstances.
	</p>
	<p>When determining the appropriate refund amount, Linkly LLC may consider:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Work already completed;</li>
		<li>Deliverables already provided;</li>
		<li>Project milestones completed;</li>
		<li>Hours or resources already dedicated to the project;</li>
		<li>Client approvals or acceptance of previous work;</li>
		<li>The original project requirements;</li>
		<li>Outstanding defects or issues;</li>
		<li>Amount of work remaining;</li>
		<li>Third-party costs;</li>
		<li>Client-requested changes;</li>
		<li>Client-caused delays; and</li>
		<li>The reason for cancellation or dissatisfaction.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		A full refund is not automatically guaranteed simply because a client is
		dissatisfied with a project or because the client changes their business
		requirements.
	</p>

	<h2 id="refunds-for-completed-work">6. Refunds for Completed Work</h2>
	<p>
		Where Linkly LLC has already completed and delivered work in accordance with
		the agreed scope, payment for that completed work is generally non-refundable.
	</p>
	<p>
		However, if the delivered work materially fails to meet the agreed
		requirements and the issue cannot reasonably be resolved, Linkly LLC may, at
		its discretion, provide an appropriate partial or full refund.
	</p>

	<h2 id="client-requested-changes">7. Client-Requested Changes</h2>
	<p>
		A refund will generally not be provided when dissatisfaction results from
		requirements, preferences, functionality, designs, or features that were not
		included in the original agreed scope.
	</p>
	<p>Requests for:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>New features;</li>
		<li>Additional functionality;</li>
		<li>Major design changes;</li>
		<li>Changes to previously approved requirements;</li>
		<li>New integrations;</li>
		<li>Additional platforms; or</li>
		<li>Other work outside the agreed scope</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		may be treated as additional work and may require a new estimate, change
		order, or additional payment.
	</p>

	<h2 id="client-responsibilities">8. Client Responsibilities and Delays</h2>
	<p>
		Clients are responsible for providing the information and cooperation
		reasonably required to complete a project, including:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Timely feedback;</li>
		<li>Approvals;</li>
		<li>Content and assets;</li>
		<li>Credentials and access;</li>
		<li>API keys;</li>
		<li>Technical information;</li>
		<li>Business requirements; and</li>
		<li>Other materials reasonably necessary for delivery.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		If project delays, missed deadlines, incomplete functionality, or
		dissatisfaction are primarily caused by client delays, changes, lack of
		cooperation, failure to provide required information, or failure to provide
		timely approvals, Linkly LLC may adjust or deny a refund request to the extent
		permitted by the applicable agreement and law.
	</p>

	<h2 id="third-party-services">9. Third-Party Services and Costs</h2>
	<p>
		Certain project expenses may be paid to third-party providers on behalf of the
		client.
	</p>
	<p>Examples include:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Cloud hosting;</li>
		<li>Domain registration;</li>
		<li>API usage;</li>
		<li>Software licenses;</li>
		<li>SaaS subscriptions;</li>
		<li>Plugins;</li>
		<li>App-store fees;</li>
		<li>Payment-processing fees;</li>
		<li>Third-party development tools; and</li>
		<li>Other external services.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		Third-party fees that have already been paid and are non-refundable by the
		relevant provider may not be refundable by Linkly LLC.
	</p>
	<p>
		Where a third-party provider issues a refund to Linkly LLC for a client-related
		expense, Linkly LLC may pass the applicable refundable amount to the client.
	</p>

	<h2 id="subscription-services">10. Subscription and Recurring Services</h2>
	<p>
		For recurring services, maintenance agreements, support plans, retainers, or
		subscriptions, cancellation and refund terms may be governed by the applicable
		service agreement or order.
	</p>
	<p>
		Unless otherwise agreed in writing, fees for services already provided during
		a billing period are generally non-refundable.
	</p>
	<p>
		Any prepaid unused services may be reviewed for a potential refund depending
		on the applicable agreement and circumstances.
	</p>

	<h2 id="deposits-and-payments">11. Deposits and Project Payments</h2>
	<p>
		Project deposits or advance payments may be used to reserve development
		resources, begin project planning, conduct discovery, create architecture,
		design systems, purchase third-party services, or commence development.
	</p>
	<p>
		Accordingly, deposits are not automatically refundable after work has begun.
	</p>
	<p>
		However, if Linkly LLC is unable to deliver a material portion of the agreed
		services, or where circumstances otherwise justify a refund, we will review the
		matter fairly and may issue a partial or full refund.
	</p>

	<h2 id="refund-processing">12. Refund Processing</h2>
	<p>
		If a refund is approved, Linkly LLC will confirm the approved amount and refund
		method in writing.
	</p>
	<p>
		Unless otherwise required by applicable law or agreed in writing, approved
		refunds will generally be issued using the original payment method.
	</p>
	<p>
		Processing times may vary depending on the payment provider, bank, card issuer,
		or other financial institution.
	</p>

	<h2 id="chargebacks">13. Chargebacks and Payment Disputes</h2>
	<p>
		If you have a concern regarding a payment, we encourage you to contact Linkly
		LLC before initiating a chargeback or payment dispute.
	</p>
	<p>
		We will make reasonable efforts to investigate and resolve legitimate payment
		concerns directly.
	</p>
	<p>
		Nothing in this policy limits any rights available to a client under applicable
		law or the rules of the applicable payment provider.
	</p>

	<h2 id="no-waiver">14. No Waiver of Legal Rights</h2>
	<p>
		Nothing in this Refund & Satisfaction Policy is intended to waive, limit, or
		eliminate any rights or remedies that cannot legally be waived under
		applicable federal, state, or local law.
	</p>
	<p>
		If a signed contract, Master Services Agreement, Statement of Work, proposal,
		or other written agreement contains specific refund, cancellation, termination,
		or payment provisions, those provisions will control to the extent of any
		conflict with this policy.
	</p>

	<h2 id="final-determination">15. Final Refund Determination</h2>
	<p>
		Each refund request will be evaluated individually and in good faith.
	</p>
	<p>
		Linkly LLC will consider the facts and circumstances of the specific engagement,
		including the applicable contract, project scope, work completed, client
		communications, approvals, outstanding issues, and applicable law.
	</p>
	<p>
		Where a refund is approved, Linkly LLC will provide the client with written
		confirmation of the approved amount and applicable processing details.
	</p>

	<h2 id="good-faith-requests">16. Good-Faith Refund Requests</h2>
	<p>
		Clients will not be penalized merely for submitting a legitimate refund request
		in good faith.
	</p>
	<p>
		We encourage clients to communicate concerns as soon as they arise so that
		Linkly LLC has a reasonable opportunity to investigate and resolve the matter.
	</p>

	<h2 id="contact-us">17. Contact Us</h2>
	<p>
		If you have questions about this Refund & Satisfaction Policy or wish to submit
		a refund request, please contact:
	</p>
	<p>
		<strong>Linkly LLC</strong><br />
		<strong>Email:</strong>
		<a href="mailto:payment@linklyLLC.com">payment@linklyLLC.com</a><br />
		<strong>Phone:</strong> +1 224-202-7114<br />
		<strong>Website:</strong>
		<a href="https://linkly-llc.com/">https://linkly-llc.com/</a>
	</p>
	<p>
		By engaging Linkly LLC for services, clients acknowledge that the applicable
		project agreement, Statement of Work, proposal, or service terms may contain
		additional provisions governing payments, cancellations, refunds, and
		termination.
	</p>
	<p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> October 6, 2026</p>
</LegalLayout>

<footer class="legal-signature">
	<p>
		<strong>{company}</strong><br />
		<strong>Email:</strong>
		<a href="mailto:payment@linklyLLC.com">payment@linklyLLC.com</a><br />
		<strong>Phone:</strong> +1 224-202-7114<br />
		<strong>Website:</strong>
		<a href={site.url}>{site.url.replace(/^https?:\/\//, '')}</a><br />
		<strong>Address:</strong>
		{
			addressLines.map(line => (
				<>
					{line}
					<br />
				</>
			))
		}
	</p>
</footer>

<style>
	.legal-signature {
		container-type: inline-size;
		width: min(100% - 2 * var(--gutter, 1.25rem), 72rem);
		margin-inline: auto;
		margin-block: 2rem 3rem;
		padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--theme-border);
		border-radius: var(--border-radius-sm);
		background: var(--theme-surface-1);
	}

	.legal-signature p {
		margin: 0;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	.legal-signature a {
		color: var(--color-brand-ink);
	}
</style>
